#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.3 Measurement {#33-measurement}"
msgstr "3.3 Pengukuran {#33-measurement}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurement is theoretically a very complicated topic. But in practical terms, making a measurement along $z$ (as all IBM&reg; quantum computers do) simply forces the qubit’s state $\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle \\quad (s.t.|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1)$ either to $|0\\rangle$ or to $|1\\rangle$, and we observe the outcome.\n"
"- $|\\alpha|^2$ is the probability we will get $|0\\rangle$ when we measure.\n"
"- $|\\beta|^2$ is the probability we will get $|1\\rangle$ when we measure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran secara teori adalah topik yang sangat rumit. Tapi secara praktis, melakukan pengukuran sepanjang $z$ (seperti yang dilakukan semua komputer kuantum IBM&reg;) hanya memaksa kondisi qubit $\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle \\quad (s.t.|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1)$ menjadi $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$, dan kita mengamati hasilnya.\n"
"- $|\\alpha|^2$ adalah probabilitas kita mendapatkan $|0\\rangle$ saat mengukur.\n"
"- $|\\beta|^2$ adalah probabilitas kita mendapatkan $|1\\rangle$ saat mengukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are called probability amplitudes. (see \"Born rule\")\n"
msgstr "Jadi, $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ disebut amplitudo probabilitas. (lihat \"aturan Born\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|1\\rangle$ has an equal probability of becoming $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ upon measurement. $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}|0\\rangle-\\frac{1}{2}i|1\\rangle$ has a 75% chance of becoming $|0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|1\\rangle$ memiliki probabilitas yang sama untuk menjadi $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$ saat diukur. $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}|0\\rangle-\\frac{1}{2}i|1\\rangle$ memiliki peluang 75% untuk menjadi $|0\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Aer Simulator {#qiskit-aer-simulator}"
msgstr "Qiskit Aer Simulator {#qiskit-aer-simulator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, let's measure a circuit that prepares the equal probability superposition above.\n"
"We should add the measurement gates, as the Qiskit Aer simulator simulates an ideal (with no noise) quantum hardware by default. Note: The Aer simulator can also apply a noise model based on real quantum computer. We will return to noise models later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, mari kita ukur sebuah circuit yang menyiapkan superposisi probabilitas sama di atas.\n"
"Kita perlu menambahkan gate pengukuran, karena Qiskit Aer simulator mensimulasikan perangkat keras kuantum ideal (tanpa noise) secara default. Catatan: Simulator Aer juga bisa menerapkan model noise berdasarkan komputer kuantum nyata. Kita akan kembali ke model noise nanti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/3956e602-9f1b-4083-b58d-26c91b50b75e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/3956e602-9f1b-4083-b58d-26c91b50b75e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We are now ready to run our circuit on the Aer simulator. In this example, we will apply the default shots=1024, which means we will measure 1024 times. Then we will plot those counts in a histogram.\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang siap untuk menjalankan circuit kita pada simulator Aer. Dalam contoh ini, kita akan menggunakan shots=1024 secara default, yang berarti kita akan mengukur sebanyak 1024 kali. Kemudian kita akan memplot hitungan tersebut dalam histogram.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7cb7c5ab-7b12-4f77-aaca-1d7e6cff213c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7cb7c5ab-7b12-4f77-aaca-1d7e6cff213c-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that 0s and 1s were measured with a probability of almost 50% each. Although noise has not been simulated here, the states are still probabilistic. So while we expect roughly a 50-50 distribution, we will rarely find exactly that. Just as 100 flips of a coin would rarely yield exactly 50 instances of each side.\n"
msgstr "Kita melihat bahwa 0 dan 1 diukur dengan probabilitas hampir 50% masing-masing. Meskipun noise tidak disimulasikan di sini, kondisinya tetap bersifat probabilistik. Jadi meskipun kita mengharapkan distribusi kira-kira 50-50, kita jarang menemukan tepat seperti itu. Sama seperti 100 lemparan koin yang jarang menghasilkan tepat 50 masing-masing sisi.\n"

